@startuml
title 02 — Planning & Task Routing

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Triggered when the Orchestrator's background worker picks up
' the "begin planning" job that was queued in Diagram 01.
'
' The Orchestrator first checks if the conversation is a sub-conversation
' (tied to a specific active Business Agent). 
'   - If YES: it skips planning and dispatches directly to the agent.
'   - If NO: it runs safety checks, discovers agents, plans tasks, 
'     and then dispatches.
'
' Next: Diagram 05 — Business Agent Execution & Result Handling
' Errors: Diagram 10 — Guardrails & Error Handling
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

hide footbox
autonumber "<b>[00]"

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam wrapWidth 260
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor        #2D6A9F
  ArrowFontColor    #2D6A9F
  ArrowFontSize     11

  LifeLineBorderColor         #2D6A9F
  LifeLineBackgroundColor     #EAF3FB

  ParticipantBorderColor      #2D6A9F
  ParticipantBackgroundColor  #DAEAF7
  ParticipantFontColor        #1A3A52
  ParticipantFontSize         12
  ParticipantFontStyle        bold
  ParticipantPadding          8
  ParticipantBorderThickness  1.5

  GroupBorderColor            #5A9ABF
  GroupBackgroundColor        #F0F7FC
  GroupHeaderFontColor        #1A3A52
  GroupHeaderFontSize         12
  GroupBorderThickness        1.2

  NoteBackgroundColor         #FFF8DC
  NoteBorderColor             #C8A800
  NoteFontColor               #4A3800
  NoteFontSize                11
}

' ─── Participants ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
participant Orch     as "Orchestrator\n(background worker)"
database    DB       as "HANA DB"
participant Registry as "Agent Registry"
queue       Q        as "Agent Queue"
participant Push     as "Push Gateway"

' ─── Entry ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
note over Orch
  The background worker has just picked up a "begin planning"
  job from the Orchestrator's own queue channel.
end note

' ─── Routing Check ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
Orch -> DB : get conversation shared state\n(Check for main_conv_id)
DB --> Orch : shared state metadata

alt #EAF0FA Sub-Conversation (Active Business Agent session)

  note over Orch
    This conversation is tied to an active Business Agent 
    (main_conv_id is present). Skip validation/planning and 
    forward directly to the agent queue.
  end note
  
  Orch -> Q : publish "sub:user:chat" event to Agent Topic\n(Assigned Business Agent resumes its workflow)
  Q --> Orch : acknowledged

else #EAF6EA Main Conversation (New Request or Base Thread)

  Orch -> Push : send "I received your request\nand am working on it..." to user

  ' ─── Validation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  note over Orch
    Before any planning begins, the Orchestrator runs two checks:
    (1) Does this user have permission to use the system?
    (2) Is the message content safe and within policy?
  end note

  Orch -> Orch : [Validation] check user permission\n+ check message content safety

  alt #FDF3F3 Blocked — permission denied or message rejected
    Orch -> Push : send error response to user\n(see Diagram 06 for error codes)

  else #EAF6EA Allowed — proceed with planning

    ' ─── Agent Discovery ───────────────────────────────────────────────
    Orch -> Registry : fetch all active, published Business Agents\n(with their names, capabilities, and workflows)
    Registry --> Orch : list of available agents

    ' ─── AI Planning ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
    note over Orch
      The Orchestrator calls its built-in AI (LLM) twice:

      [AI call 1 — Strategy]
      Produces a plain-language summary of the goal
      and a short title for this conversation.

      [AI call 2 — Task Breakdown]
      Breaks strategy into a concrete list of tasks,
      assigning each to the best-matching Business Agent.
    end note

    Orch -> Orch : [AI call 1] analyse request\nand produce an execution strategy
    Orch -> DB   : save conversation title\n(derived from the strategy summary)

    Orch -> Orch : [AI call 2] break strategy into tasks;\nassign each task to a Business Agent

    Orch -> DB   : save full task plan\n(task list, agent assignments, order, dependencies)

    ' ─── Dispatch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    alt #EAF6EA At least one task was produced
      Orch -> DB : save user message as a conversation event
      Orch -> Q  : publish "conversation.plan.created" to Agent Topic\n(the assigned Business Agent will pick this up)
      Orch -> Push : send progress update to user\n"Working on your request..."

    else #FFF4E5 No tasks could be produced
      Orch -> Push : send "Your request is not currently\nsupported — please try rephrasing"
    end

  end
end

@enduml